title bar -> toggle Bypass off.\nOrder rule: scene = image 1 (group 1), person = image 2 (here)."], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "Note", "title": "Enable for two-image edits", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#653", "size": [520, 210], "pos": [640, 1130], "id": 102, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "Note"}, "order": 7}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#432", "widgets_values": ["Write the edit in plain English:\n  'Relight the scene with warm golden hour sunlight.'\n  'Place this person at the cafe table, holding a coffee.'\n  'Change her outfit to a red raincoat.'\n\nUnique face coming out generic? Append:\n  'Preserve the exact facial identity - distinguishing features: ...'\nand describe what makes the face distinctive.\n\ngrounding_px: how large the model 'sees' the input while reading your\ninstruction. 384-768 is the trained range. Getting doubled/split\ncompositions? LOWER it. The collapsed node below is the negative -\nonly used at CFG > 1; keep its prompt empty."], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "Note", "title": "Writing instructions", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#653", "size": [620, 300], "pos": [1620, 360], "id": 103, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "Note"}, "order": 8}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#432", "widgets_values": ["THE FIDELITY DIAL (ref_boost) - how hard the model looks at your\nreference. New in this release.\n\n  1.0 = classic v1.1 behavior\n  4.0 = recommended (pre-set): much stronger face + body likeness,\n        more reliable edits\n  >10 = over-copy: removals/replacements start failing\n  <1  = suppress the reference (creative freedom)\n\nref_boost_a: the scene dial (image 1) in two-image mode -\nleave at 1.0 unless you are exploring. ref_boost applies to the\nperson (image 2) when group 2 is enabled, else to your image.\n\nfit_mode: how inputs fit a different output aspect\nratio. fit = resample to the output shape (default, recommended); crop (legacy) = center-crop\nonly for v1/v1.1 weights."], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "Note", "title": "Fidelity dial", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#653", "size": [420, 420], "pos": [2320, 230], "id": 104, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "Note"}, "order": 9}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#432", "widgets_values": ["Turbo model: 10 steps, cfg 1.\n\nStep dial:\n  8  = stronger composition/instruction adherence\n  12 = more face detail\n  10 = balanced\n\nUsing krea2_raw instead of turbo:\n40 steps, cfg 3-4 (negative then matters)."], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "Note", "title": "Sampling", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#653", "size": [320, 280], "pos": [2800, 490], "id": 105, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "Note"}, "order": 10}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#232", "widgets_values": ["KREA 2 IDENTITY EDIT  -  v1.2 (Fidelity update)\nUse an image like a LoRA: your character/scene goes in as a reference, plain-English\ninstructions do the rest.\n\nQUICK START:  1) load your image in group 1   2) write the instruction in group 3   3) Queue.\nThe Fidelity dial (group 4) ships at 4 = strong likeness. Two-image person-into-scene: enable\ngroup 2 (right-click its title -> toggle Bypass).\n\nRequires the comfyui-krea2edit nodes from this release or newer.\ngithub.com/lbouaraba/comfyui-krea2edit   -   huggingface.co/conradlocke/krea2-identity-edit"], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "Note", "title": "README", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#353", "size": [1600, 330], "pos": [620, -600], "id": 106, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "Note"}, "order": 11}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#432", "widgets_values": ["Output resolution. 1MP is the\nsweet spot; go higher only for\nsingle-person edits."], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "Note", "title": "Resolution", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#653", "size": [270, 110], "pos": [1250, -140], "id": 107, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "Note"}, "order": 12}, {"mode": 0, "outp